## 🔥 STEP 1: Set Up Firestore Collection (One-Time)

### 1.1 Open Firebase Console

Go to: **https://console.firebase.google.com/**

Select your project: **showroom-management-syst-6a941**

### 1.2 Enable Firestore (if not already)

1. In the left sidebar → Click **"Firestore Database"**
2. If it shows "Create database" → Click it
3. Choose **"Start in production mode"**
4. Select location closest to Pakistan → **asia-south1 (Mumbai)** recommended
5. Click **"Enable"**

### 1.3 Set Security Rules

1. In Firestore → Click the **"Rules"** tab
2. Replace the default rules with:

```javascript
rules_version = '2';
service cloud.firestore {
  match /databases/{database}/documents {
    match /allowed_devices/{deviceId} {
      allow read: if true;
      allow write: if false;
    }
    match /{document=**} {
      allow read, write: if false;
    }
  }
}
```

3. Click **"Publish"**

